	(text "LA pull-ups and pull-downs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b2a7cbba-59c4-4579-9759-41792aac329e")
	)
	(text "U54 TCA6416A at 0x21 (ADDR = VCCP). Each port drives one resistor to the J1 side of the LSF0108 (An_B):\nport high = pull-up, low = pull-down, input = off. Port supply = VREF_OUT, so the pulls follow the I/O voltage\n(1.8 / 3.3 / 5 V); in 5 V mode a pull-up lifts a pod-driven high from about 3.3 V to 5 V.\nReplaces U18-U21 (SN74LVC2G66 on the FPGA side) and the TCA9554 at 0x20: old firmware gets a NACK, pulls stay off.\nPULL_RST (PG7) low = expander in reset, all ports inputs, pulls off. R64 holds it low while the STM32 boots;\nfirmware turns VREF_OUT on first, then releases PULL_RST (TI: ramp VCCP before VCCI, else SDA can stick low).\nLA1/2 4.7k, LA3/4 2.2k, LA5-8 10k (as before, now up or down), LA9-14 2.2k (new)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1fd8999f-6349-47f6-a56e-deb6eb5699bb")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
